      "notes": "\n<h2>Plant Tissue</h2>\n\n<h3>What is plant tissue?</h3>\n\n<p>\nPlant tissue is a group of plant cells that work together to perform\na particular function.\n</p>\n\n<h3>Why do plants need different tissues?</h3>\n\n<p>\nPlants perform many different functions, including transporting water,\ntransporting sugars, carrying out photosynthesis and protecting\ninternal tissues.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nDifferent tissues are specialised for these different functions.\n</p>\n\n<h3>Example: xylem tissue</h3>\n\n<p>\nXylem tissue is specialised for transporting water and mineral salts\nthrough the plant.\n</p>\n\n<h3>Worked example</h3>\n\n<p><b>Question:</b> Why is xylem considered a tissue rather than a\nsingle cell?</p>\n\n<p><b>Step 1:</b> Xylem is made from many specialised cells and vessel\nelements.</p>\n\n<p><b>Step 2:</b> These structures work together in water transport.</p>\n\n<p><b>Answer:</b> Xylem is a tissue because multiple specialised\nstructures work together to perform transport.</p>\n  ",
