      "notes": "\n  <h2>Homozygous Dominant and Homozygous Recessive</h2>\n\n  <h3>Homozygous dominant</h3>\n\n  <p>\n    A genotype is <b>homozygous dominant</b> when both alleles are dominant.\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    Example:\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    <b>AA</b>\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    Both alleles are A, and A is dominant.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Homozygous recessive</h3>\n\n  <p>\n    A genotype is <b>homozygous recessive</b> when both alleles are recessive.\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    Example:\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    <b>aa</b>\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    Both alleles are a, and a is recessive.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Step-by-step identification</h3>\n\n  <p>\n    Consider <b>AA</b>.\n  </p>\n\n  <ol>\n    <li>The two alleles are the same → homozygous.</li>\n    <li>Both alleles are dominant → dominant.</li>\n    <li>Therefore → homozygous dominant.</li>\n  </ol>\n\n  <p>\n    Consider <b>aa</b>.\n  </p>\n\n  <ol>\n    <li>The two alleles are the same → homozygous.</li>\n    <li>Both alleles are recessive → recessive.</li>\n    <li>Therefore → homozygous recessive.</li>\n  </ol>\n\n  <h3>Quick comparison</h3>\n\n  <p>\n    <b>AA</b> → homozygous dominant\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    <b>Aa</b> → heterozygous\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    <b>aa</b> → homozygous recessive\n  </p>\n  ",
