      "notes": "\n  <h2>Rhesus Factor Cross: RR × rr</h2>\n\n  <p>\n    Consider a cross between an Rh-positive parent with genotype <b>RR</b>\n    and an Rh-negative parent with genotype <b>rr</b>.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Step 1: Write the parental genotypes</h3>\n\n  <p>\n    <b>RR × rr</b>\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Step 2: Find the gametes</h3>\n\n  <p>\n    The RR parent can produce only <b>R</b> gametes.\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    The rr parent can produce only <b>r</b> gametes.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Step 3: Combine the alleles</h3>\n\n  <p>\n    Every offspring receives R from the first parent and r from the second.\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    Therefore every offspring has:\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    <b>Rr</b>\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Step 4: Determine the phenotype</h3>\n\n  <p>\n    Rr is Rh positive in the simplified model.\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    Therefore:\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n    <b>100% of the offspring are predicted to be Rh positive.</b>\n  </p>\n  ",
