      "notes": "\n  <h2>Class to Order</h2>\n\n  <h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>\n\n  <p>\n  An <b>order</b> is a taxonomic rank below class and above family.\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n  A class contains several orders. Organisms within an order share more\n  specific characteristics than all organisms in the wider class.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Example</h3>\n\n  <p>\n  Humans belong to the class <b>Mammalia</b>.\n  Within Mammalia, humans belong to the order <b>Primates</b>.\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n  Primates include humans, apes, monkeys and other related animals.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>The hierarchy</h3>\n\n  <p>\n  <b>Kingdom → Phylum → Class → Order</b>\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n  Each step downward reduces the number of organisms in the group and\n  increases specificity.\n  ",
