      "notes": "\n  <h2>Family to Genus</h2>\n\n  <h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>\n\n  <p>\n  A <b>genus</b> is a taxonomic rank below family and above species.\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n  A genus contains one or more closely related species.\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Example</h3>\n\n  <p>\n  Humans belong to the genus <b>Homo</b>.\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n  Our species is <b>Homo sapiens</b>.\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n  Therefore:\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n  <b>Family Hominidae → Genus Homo → Species Homo sapiens</b>\n  </p>\n\n  <h3>Why genus is important</h3>\n\n  <p>\n  Members of the same genus are more closely related than organisms that\n  are grouped only within the same family.\n  </p>\n\n  <p>\n  The genus is also the first part of a scientific name in binomial\n  nomenclature.\n  ",
