      "notes": "\n<h2>Habitat</h2>\n\n<p>\nA <b>habitat</b> is the place where an organism normally lives and obtains the conditions and resources it needs.\n</p>\n\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n\n<p>\nDifferent organisms have different habitats.\n</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>A fish may live in a lake.</li>\n<li>A camel may live in a dry region.</li>\n<li>A frog may live in or around freshwater environments.</li>\n<li>A tree may grow in a forest.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>What makes a habitat suitable?</h3>\n\n<p>\nA suitable habitat must provide the organism with the conditions and resources required for survival and reproduction.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nThese may include:\n</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>food</li>\n<li>water</li>\n<li>suitable temperature</li>\n<li>shelter</li>\n<li>space</li>\n<li>breeding conditions</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Important distinction</h3>\n\n<p>\nA habitat is the <b>place</b> where an organism lives.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nIt should not be confused with a niche, which describes the organism's role and way of using resources within its environment.\n</p>\n",
