      "notes": "\n<h2>Carnivores</h2>\n\n<p>\nA <b>carnivore</b> is a consumer that feeds mainly on other animals.\n</p>\n\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n\n<ul>\n<li>lion</li>\n<li>cheetah</li>\n<li>hawk</li>\n<li>snake</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Position in a food chain</h3>\n\n<p>\nCarnivores may feed on herbivores or on other consumers.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nFor example:\n</p>\n\n<p>\n<b>Grass → zebra → lion</b>\n</p>\n\n<p>\nThe lion is a carnivore because it feeds on the zebra.\n</p>\n\n<h3>Predator and carnivore are not identical terms</h3>\n\n<p>\nA predator is an organism that captures and feeds on prey.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nCarnivore describes an organism's feeding type: it mainly eats animals.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nA carnivore may therefore act as a predator, but the two words describe different ideas.\n",
