      "notes": "\n<h2>Omnivores</h2>\n\n<p>\nAn <b>omnivore</b> is a consumer that feeds on both plant material and animal material.\n</p>\n\n<h3>Examples</h3>\n\n<p>\nHumans are omnivores because humans can obtain food from both plants and animals.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nSome other animals also have diets containing both plant and animal material.\n</p>\n\n<h3>Why classification depends on diet</h3>\n\n<p>\nThe classification describes what the organism normally eats.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nAn animal does not have to eat equal amounts of plants and animals to be an omnivore.\n</p>\n\n<h3>Compare</h3>\n\n<p>\n<b>Herbivore:</b> mainly plant material.\n</p>\n\n<p>\n<b>Carnivore:</b> mainly animal material.\n</p>\n\n<p>\n<b>Omnivore:</b> both plant and animal material.\n</p>\n",
