      "notes": "\n<h2>Carbon Balance and Human Activities</h2>\n\n<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>\n\n<p>\nThe carbon cycle contains processes that transfer carbon into the atmosphere\nand processes that remove carbon from the atmosphere.\n</p>\n\n<h3>PROCESSES THAT RELEASE CARBON DIOXIDE</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Respiration</li>\n  <li>Decomposition</li>\n  <li>Combustion</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>PROCESSES THAT REMOVE ATMOSPHERIC CARBON DIOXIDE</h3>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Photosynthesis</li>\n  <li>Absorption by oceans and other water bodies</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>HUMAN IMPACT</h3>\n\n<p>\nHuman activities can alter the balance of carbon transfers.\n</p>\n\n<p>\nBurning fossil fuels transfers large amounts of stored carbon into the\natmosphere.\nDeforestation can also reduce the amount of carbon dioxide removed by\nphotosynthesis because fewer plants are available to photosynthesise.\n</p>\n\n<h3>WORKED REASONING</h3>\n\n<p><strong>Question:</strong> Why can deforestation contribute to increased atmospheric carbon dioxide?</p>\n\n<p>\n<strong>Step 1:</strong> Living plants remove carbon dioxide through photosynthesis.</p>\n\n<p>\n<strong>Step 2:</strong> Removing many plants reduces the amount of photosynthesis\ntaking place.</p>\n\n<p>\n<strong>Step 3:</strong> The carbon dioxide removal rate can therefore decrease.</p>\n\n<p>\n<strong>Step 4:</strong> If carbon dioxide continues to be released by processes\nsuch as combustion and respiration, atmospheric carbon dioxide can increase.\n</p>\n\n<h3>IMPORTANT</h3>\n\n<p>\nThe carbon cycle itself is natural.\nThe concern is that human activities can alter the rates of particular carbon\ntransfers and therefore disturb the balance.\n</p>\n",
