      "notes": "\n<h2>Drawing a Conclusion from Plant Growth Data</h2>\n\n<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>\n\n<p>A scientific conclusion should be based directly on the evidence collected.</p>\n\n<h3>Example</h3>\n\n<p>A student investigates temperature and seedling growth.</p>\n\n<p>Mean growth rates are:</p>\n\n<p>15°C → 0.8 cm/day</p>\n\n<p>25°C → 1.6 cm/day</p>\n\n<p>35°C → 1.2 cm/day</p>\n\n<h3>Step 1: Identify the Pattern</h3>\n\n<p>Growth rate increases from 15°C to 25°C.</p>\n\n<p>Growth rate then decreases at 35°C.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 2: Identify the Highest Tested Value</h3>\n\n<p>25°C gives the highest measured growth rate.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 3: Write the Conclusion</h3>\n\n<p>Under the conditions tested, seedling growth rate was highest at 25°C.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 4: Avoid Overclaiming</h3>\n\n<p>It would be too strong to say that 25°C is the optimum temperature for all plants.</p>\n\n<p>The evidence only supports the tested species and experimental conditions.</p>\n\n<h3>Exam Structure</h3>\n\n<p><strong>State the pattern → quote relevant data → give a limited conclusion.</strong></p>\n  \n<hr>\n\n<h2>Drawing a Conclusion from Plant Growth Data</h2>\n\n<h3>DEEP NOTES</h3>\n\n<p>A scientific conclusion should be based directly on the evidence collected.</p>\n\n<h3>Example</h3>\n\n<p>A student investigates temperature and seedling growth.</p>\n\n<p>Mean growth rates are:</p>\n\n<p>15°C → 0.8 cm/day</p>\n\n<p>25°C → 1.6 cm/day</p>\n\n<p>35°C → 1.2 cm/day</p>\n\n<h3>Step 1: Identify the Pattern</h3>\n\n<p>Growth rate increases from 15°C to 25°C.</p>\n\n<p>Growth rate then decreases at 35°C.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 2: Identify the Highest Tested Value</h3>\n\n<p>25°C gives the highest measured growth rate.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 3: Write the Conclusion</h3>\n\n<p>Under the conditions tested, seedling growth rate was highest at 25°C.</p>\n\n<h3>Step 4: Avoid Overclaiming</h3>\n\n<p>It would be too strong to say that 25°C is the optimum temperature for all plants.</p>\n\n<p>The evidence only supports the tested species and experimental conditions.</p>\n\n<h3>Exam Structure</h3>\n\n<p><strong>State the pattern → quote relevant data → give a limited conclusion.</strong></p>\n  ",
